IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-interpretation`
IMPORT `g6-art15-16-deregistration`
IMPORT `g6-art17-after-deregistration`
IMPORT `g6-art18-governor-duties`
IMPORT `g6-art20-court-orders`
IMPORT `g6-art19-reportable-matters`

-- g6-tests-red.l4: tests that are MEANT TO FAIL, and are counted: 24 assertions, one for each fork of the register, each failing.
-- Each asserts, on the discriminating case of its fork, the answer of the reading NOT taken, evaluated under `the readings taken`. The reading taken answers the other way, so the assertion fails;
-- that is the point. The file shows where the readings part ways (the expected failures are the register's discriminating cases), and it proves the harness can fail: if a reading
-- taken were changed, an assertion here would start to pass and the count in check.sh would no longer hold.
-- Every expectation below is the one the register gives for the other reading, decided from the text; none was edited to match what the code computes.
-- Expected failed assertions: 24 (check.sh, expected_failed table).

§ `Tests that are meant to fail`

§§ `Fixtures`

`a company charity` MEANS Entity WITH
    name IS "Hope Limited"
    `standing on the register` IS `entered in the general section`
    `kinds of entity` IS LIST `a company`
    `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
    governors IS EMPTY
    purposes IS EMPTY

`Eve aware and conceals` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Eve", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`Gil encourages Hui` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Gil", FALSE, FALSE, (LIST "Hui"), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`Hui refuses and does nothing` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Hui", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the board of Gil and Hui` MEANS LIST `Gil encourages Hui`, `Hui refuses and does nothing`

`a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable` MEANS `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 31), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 2 March 2026, the time not reasonable` MEANS `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 2), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a notice on the charity, steps due by 31 December 2026, not complied with` MEANS `Required steps notice` OF `the registered charity`, `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`, (YMD 2026 1 15), JUST (YMD 2026 12 31), FALSE, FALSE

`the route of a deregistration for misleading` MEANS `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity`
`a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in both notices` MEANS `Deregistration of the entity` OF `the route of a deregistration for misleading`, (YMD 2026 4 1), (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)), (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), TRUE
`a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` MEANS `Deregistration of the entity` OF `the route of a deregistration for misleading`, (YMD 2026 6 1), NOTHING, (JUST (YMD 2021 6 1)), (JUST (YMD 2021 6 1)), NOTHING, TRUE
`a donation received on 1 June 2025, between the past date and the notice, that remains` MEANS `Property of the charity` OF "a donation", (YMD 2025 6 1), TRUE

`Pat once disqualified as a charity trustee` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Pat", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, (LIST (`Disqualification elsewhere` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), JUST (YMD 2015 1 1))), EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE

`position of Gus: reported to the charity only, on 12 March` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 1), JUST (YMD 2026 3 12), NOTHING, TRUE, FALSE
`position of Gus: the matter arose on 1 March 2026, he became aware on 20 March, and reported to both on 25 March` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 20), JUST (YMD 2026 3 25), JUST (YMD 2026 3 25), TRUE, FALSE
`ten days` MEANS JUST 10
`Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, no declaration yet` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(4)` OF (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)), NOTHING, FALSE
`Gwen with no reportable matter` MEANS Governor WITH
    name IS "Gwen"
    `is a natural person` IS TRUE
    `is resident in Jersey` IS TRUE
    `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS FALSE
    `reportable matters` IS EMPTY
`position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 1), JUST (YMD 2026 3 12), JUST (YMD 2026 3 10), TRUE, FALSE
`a permission under Article 19(9)(e)(ii) given on 1 April 2026 with a time limit ending on 31 May` MEANS `Permission to act as a governor` OF `the Commissioner by notice entered in the register under Article 19(9)(e)(ii)`, (YMD 2026 4 1), NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST (YMD 2026 5 31)
`an order against Zed from 29 February 2028 to 1 March 2043` MEANS `Disqualification order` OF "Zed", YMD 2028 2 29, YMD 2043 3 1
`the register entry of an organized religious charity` MEANS `Registered charity` WITH
    entity IS `a company charity`
    `registration number` IS "2"
    `registered name` IS "Faith Society"
    `alternative registered names` IS EMPTY
    `date registered` IS YMD 2019 1 1
    `date deregistered` IS NOTHING
    `registered charitable purposes` IS LIST "advancement of religion"
    `registered public benefit statement` IS "worship"
    `is an organized religious charity` IS TRUE

§§ `The twenty-four expected failures, one for each fork`

-- F6.1. Entity that has not complied with Article 15(2): reading D (the Law states no rule) expects a refusal; the reading taken (no duty arises) answers FULFILLED.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 15(3) where the entity has not complied with paragraph (2)` `the readings taken`
-- F6.2. Entity that no longer exists, no preliminary notice: reading B expects the procedure of Article 16(1) not to have been followed (so no duty yet); the reading taken answers TRUE (Article 16(2) governs alone).
#ASSERT NOT   `F6.2 the procedure of Article 16(1) that Article 16(2) requires` `the readings taken` NOTHING (YMD 2026 4 1)
-- F6.3. Act on 15 March 2026 between the notices: reading B (the preliminary notice) expects it NOT protected; the reading taken protects it.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(4) the act is not rendered an offence by the retrospective effect` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in both notices` (YMD 2026 3 15)
-- F6.4. Donation between the past date and the notice: reading B expects it to be remaining property; the reading taken says it is not.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(5) the property is remaining property` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in both notices` `a donation received on 1 June 2025, between the past date and the notice, that remains`
-- F6.5. Notice 1 June 2026, effective 1 June 2021, asked on 1 January 2033: reading B expects the information may be discarded; the reading taken says it must still be retained.
#ASSERT       (YMD 2033 1 1) AT LEAST `Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner may discard the information on` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021`
-- F6.6. A reassignment attempt in year 11 (1 June 2037): reading B expects the registered number is no longer barred; the reading taken says it still is.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(1)(b) the registered number may not be assigned on the day` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` (YMD 2037 6 1)
-- F6.7. A director of a registered company charity: reading B expects the standard of care of Article 18(2) to bind; the reading taken says it does not.
#ASSERT       `Art 18(2) the governor is bound by the standard of care` `the readings taken` TRUE `a company charity`
-- F6.8. A governor conceals the misconduct for a month and then discloses it within a reasonable time: reading B expects no misconduct; the reading taken says misconduct at once.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4)(d) the governor becomes aware of misconduct and conceals it or fails to act` `the readings taken` `Eve aware and conceals`
-- F6.9. A disqualification imposed in 2010 and ended in 2015: reading B expects it is not a reportable matter in 2026; the reading taken counts it.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` `the readings taken` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Pat once disqualified as a charity trustee`
-- F6.10. Reported to the charity only, then acts on 13 March: reading B expects the ban has started; the reading taken (the report to the Commissioner) says it has not.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the charity only, on 12 March` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 13) TRUE
-- F6.11. Acting in breach of Article 19(2) or (4): reading B expects the penalty of Article 19(11); the reading taken provides none.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(8) the penalty for contravening Article 19(8)` `the readings taken` EQUALS `Penalty provided` OF (JUST 12), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`
-- F6.12. Matter arose 1 March, aware 20 March, reported 25 March, ten days count as prompt: reading B (from the matter arising) expects the report is NOT prompt; the reading taken uses the input (TRUE).
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(2) the report made on the date is prompt` `the readings taken` `ten days` `position of Gus: the matter arose on 1 March 2026, he became aware on 20 March, and reported to both on 25 March` (YMD 2026 3 25)
-- F6.13. A notice giving one day for objections: reading B (any time suffices) expects it is the notice the paragraph requires; the reading taken says it is not.
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) the preliminary notice is the notice the paragraph requires` `the readings taken` `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 2 March 2026, the time not reasonable`
-- F6.14. An order beginning on 29 February 2028 and ending on 1 March 2043: reading B (29 February rolls) expects it is within the limit; the reading taken says it is over.
#ASSERT       `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` `the readings taken` `an order against Zed from 29 February 2028 to 1 March 2043`
-- F6.15. A governor of an organized religious charity: reading C (the Law does not say) expects a refusal; the reading taken (Article 28(3) prevails) answers with the permission.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 19(9)(e)(i) the removal alternative of the Commissioner` `the readings taken` `a company charity` `the register entry of an organized religious charity`
-- F6.16. A term of 366 days from 1 March 2027 under Article 19(11): reading B (days) expects it is over the maximum; the reading taken (12 calendar months) says it is within.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(11) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of one year` `the readings taken` (YMD 2027 3 1) 366
-- F6.17. Notice given 1 March, objections until 31 March, deregistration on 15 March: reading A (at any time after the notice) expects it is allowed; the reading taken waits for the last day.
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) the time for objections allows deregistration on the day` `the readings taken` `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable` (YMD 2026 3 15)
-- F6.18. Ten years from 1 June 2026: reading C (the day before the anniversary) expects the last day is 31 May 2036; the reading taken says 1 June 2036.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(1)(a) the last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` EQUALS YMD 2036 5 31
-- F6.19. A notice due on 31 December 2026, not yet complied with, asked on 1 March 2026: reading B (whenever the steps are not yet taken) expects it is failed; the reading taken says it is not.
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` `the readings taken` (LIST `a notice on the charity, steps due by 31 December 2026, not complied with`) (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- F6.20. A declaration given on the day of the application: reading B (an earlier day) expects it is not in time; the reading taken says it is.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(3) the declaration was provided before the application was made` `the readings taken` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 10)) (YMD 2026 5 10)
-- F6.21. Notified on 1 June, asked on 2 June, no declaration, no reasonable time said to have passed: reading B expects no breach yet; the reading taken says in breach.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` `the readings taken` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 2) `Gwen with no reportable matter` `Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, no declaration yet`
-- F6.22. A permission with a time limit ending on 31 May: reading B expects the governor acting on 31 May contravenes paragraph (10); the reading taken says the day named is inside the permission.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission under Article 19(9)(e)(ii) given on 1 April 2026 with a time limit ending on 31 May`) (YMD 2026 5 31) TRUE
-- F6.23. It appears to the Attorney General only: reading B expects the Commissioner may apply; the reading taken says only the Commissioner's own view counts.
#ASSERT       `the view of expediency that lets the applicant apply` `the readings taken` FALSE TRUE
-- F6.24. Gil encourages Hui, who refuses: reading B expects Gil's encouragement is misconduct; the reading taken says it is not.
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` TRUE `the board of Gil and Hui` `Gil encourages Hui`
